para('Derived elementary argument; no novelty or historical-use claim. Let H be a Frobenius-stable cyclic subgroup of odd prime order ell, with Frobenius scalar lambda. Let K be its monic half-kernel polynomial and S1 its root sum.')
para('If a different scalar k has the same complete y-function, a=k/lambda preserves y on every nonidentity point. Its orbits fit in fibers of a cubic, so their size is at most three. Order two is impossible: a=-1 reverses y, and a nonidentity odd-order point cannot have y=0. Thus a has order three and ell is 1 modulo 3.')
